WEBVTT

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:09.426
A NETFLIX ORIGINAL ANIME SERIES

00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:15.974
ORIGINAL WORK BY KOUSUKE OONO

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:19.811
PRODUCED BY NETFLIX

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:43.686
EPISODE 37

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.147
Crepes aren't bringing in
the dough these days.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.317
Might be time for a new menu… Huh?

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:51.319
Oh, yeah, what's that again?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.698
They're popular nowadays.
What are they called again? Um…

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:59.828
Right! Tapioca!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.288
It's tapioca milk tea!

00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:05.792
<i>You're the only one
who knows this stuff around here.</i>

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:08.711
Though I'm pissed, I have to ask you.

00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:11.214
What is it?

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.677
Tell me everything you know about tapioca.

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:20.014
Springy texture, soft and chewy.

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:24.102
Works great in a drink.
Gets the likes on Instagram.

00:02:24.894 --> 00:02:26.855
That's tapioca.

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:27.981
Come with me.

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:31.943
Hey, tipster.
I want ingredients for tapioca balls.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.988
You better speak up!

00:02:35.071 --> 00:02:35.905
Wait.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.365
FREE GYOZA VOUCHER

00:02:37.448 --> 00:02:38.575
SMIRK

00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:40.910
Go up this building to the second floor.

00:02:42.078 --> 00:02:43.580
Is this…

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.832
a confectionary wholesaler?

00:02:45.915 --> 00:02:46.749
That is correct.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.461
They got them white powder imports
stacked up good and proper.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:52.589
Here we go.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.717
What? Flour?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.634
CRASH

00:02:56.718 --> 00:03:00.221
Tapioca comes in little balls!
Is this some kind of joke?

00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:02.682
You amateur!

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:04.809
You add hot water to it a little at a time

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:07.186
and roll it into balls yourself!

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.564
What?

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:10.481
SUPER DELICIOUS CREPES

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:14.027
Why are you just standing there?
Get the water boiling!

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.155
I'm doing it already, you fool!
Get the brown sugar ready!

00:03:17.238 --> 00:03:19.532
A little at a time!

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:21.367
I know, I'm not stupid!

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:23.286
Hey, that's too much!

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.289
ROLL

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:29.959
Hey…

00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:31.669
Yeah.

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:35.131
There it is! That's tapioca right there!

00:03:37.258 --> 00:03:39.594
More! We need to roll more!

00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:44.807
Now we just need to pour milk tea
on the tapioca balls.

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:48.019
And there you have it, tapioca milk tea!

00:03:48.102 --> 00:03:48.978
GULP

00:03:49.812 --> 00:03:51.689
SLURP

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:53.900
What happened?

00:03:56.277 --> 00:04:00.573
That tapioca ganged up on me, yo!
I took a full load right in my throat.

00:04:01.282 --> 00:04:04.285
This shit's lethal.
How can everyone be on this?

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:05.828
Okay, people, gather around.

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:09.457
This tapioca is made
from the best starch available.

00:04:10.041 --> 00:04:13.419
Once you have a lil' dabble,
there's no going back.

00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:16.172
Look, they have tapioca.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.925
No way, that's cool. I want one!

00:04:19.008 --> 00:04:20.385
GLINT

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:21.678
Uh, actually…

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.596
Yeah…

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:27.892
Excuse me.

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:31.271
Six tapioca milk teas please.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:34.524
-Tapioca.
-We have bigger sizes too.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:39.529
FREE GYOZA VOUCHER

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.446
EPISODE 38

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:46.494
We're now going to the most powerful
organization in the country.

00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:48.955
It has over 20,000 members
if you include all the branches.

00:04:49.038 --> 00:04:51.791
They will do any type of hustle.
Nothing is off-limits.

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:53.418
Any type…

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:55.378
Let's do this!

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:56.838
<i>Oh, a 100-yen shop.</i>

00:04:57.422 --> 00:04:59.549
"Bring color to your life" Seriya.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.051
"Discover amazing things" Can Goo.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.054
And this place… "Definitely" Daizo!

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.977
We got three heavyweights here,
battling it out in a turf war.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:15.857
Been a while since I've been here.
This shop's got everything

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.567
FRUIT SQUEEZER! FRESHLY SQUEEZED!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.195
But none of this stuff
feels particularly necessary either.

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:22.113
SLAP

00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:23.906
Are you looking down on housework?

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.284
The 100-yen shop is helping us out.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.369
Take this fruit squeezer, for instance.

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:29.370
SQUEEZE

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:30.872
<i>Without it…</i>

00:05:31.622 --> 00:05:32.874
<i>and with it!</i>

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:37.003
A lot of these items are useful
when you don't have much time.

00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:40.965
Say you finished cooking,
but it needs that extra something…

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:42.425
That's when…

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.428
these little 100-yen items
can really come in handy!

00:05:46.471 --> 00:05:47.430
<i>Without it… </i>

00:05:48.306 --> 00:05:49.640
<i>and with it!</i>

00:05:50.308 --> 00:05:52.351
I can see the real power
of the 100-yen shop!

00:05:52.935 --> 00:05:54.395
You know your stuff, Boss!

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:59.400
Masa, are you really doing
your housework properly?

00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:03.112
Well, yeah, of course…

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.864
Look me in the face then.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:09.869
You washing your sheets regularly?
Are you sorting out your trash?

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:11.829
Who do you think I am?

00:06:11.913 --> 00:06:12.789
PASS

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.752
Okay, so what's that then? 3, 2, 1…

00:06:17.835 --> 00:06:19.754
It's a portable insect net!

00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:22.381
It's a lint catcher
for the washing machine.

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.759
Oh, so that's what it's for.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.677
Okay, then what's this?

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:28.763
That's easy.

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.140
It's a handle for something.

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:33.059
It's an apple cutter!

00:06:33.142 --> 00:06:34.977
I was just about to say that.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:38.064
-What's this?
-Oh, yes. Right.

00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:39.315
I can see what it says there.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:40.483
This.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:44.362
Erm, this is…
I don't even need to say. It's obvious.

00:06:45.154 --> 00:06:46.989
Insect catcher!

00:06:52.495 --> 00:06:54.372
I'm sorry, Boss.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.751
I'll be honest,
I haven't been doing my housework.

00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:03.464
I thought as much.

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:06.717
Just start and take it slow.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.010
Boss…

00:07:09.053 --> 00:07:11.430
You should buy this stuff,
because it's all useful.

00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:12.348
Okay!

00:07:14.892 --> 00:07:17.311
<i>Well… What's this again?</i>

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.277
STAB

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:25.945
WAKE

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:32.160
Huh? Are you still up?

00:07:33.744 --> 00:07:35.163
PACKING CORD

00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:38.833
BOOK YOMIYA

00:07:38.916 --> 00:07:42.086
<i>What? The guy we asked can't come now?</i>

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.338
<i>Yeah, we just got the call yesterday.</i>

00:07:44.922 --> 00:07:47.592
The manager has been
desperately calling people for help.

00:07:47.675 --> 00:07:50.136
Oh, so that explains why he's here…

00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:52.722
Gather round and watch, ladies and gents.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:55.558
It's time for a picture-story show.

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.685
-Yay!
-What are you going to read?

00:07:58.269 --> 00:08:00.396
Today, I'll be reading
something I cooked up.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:02.648
Momotaro.

00:08:02.732 --> 00:08:05.193
-Oh, I know this story.
-Momotaro!

00:08:05.276 --> 00:08:06.402
That writing is extreme.

00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:12.158
<i>Once upon a time,
Boss and Boss Lady lived in a village.</i>

00:08:13.284 --> 00:08:15.453
They both went out daily
to do their own hustle.

00:08:15.536 --> 00:08:17.663
Boss would gather wood in the mountains

00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:20.500
while Boss Lady
washed clothes in the river.

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:22.668
-"Boss"?
-"Boss Lady"?

00:08:23.252 --> 00:08:26.964
<i>One day, Boss Lady came back pale-faced,</i>

00:08:27.048 --> 00:08:29.383
<i>carrying some peachy goods on her back…</i>

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:32.428
<i>"Where did you find this?"</i>

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:34.597
<i>"It's better not to ask."</i>

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:37.058
<i>"Bring me my steel."</i>

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:41.187
Boss split the goods in half
with one strike.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:44.607
Inside, a healthy-looking
baby boy was crying.

00:08:45.107 --> 00:08:49.529
"Since you were born from a peach,
we'll name you Momotaro."

00:08:49.612 --> 00:08:54.283
Momotaro grew up quickly
into a fine young man.

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:58.788
<i>"We've had some demons
messing on our turf recently."</i>

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:03.543
<i>"I can't allow them to bring dishonor
on the two of you."</i>

00:09:03.626 --> 00:09:05.920
<i>"I will spearhead an attack on them."</i>

00:09:06.003 --> 00:09:08.714
<i>"It makes us happy to hear you
say those words, Momotaro."</i>

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:12.134
<i>"Hey, Granny, get the sword
and the sweet dumplings ready."</i>

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:18.182
Momotaro leaves for Demon Island.
On the way, he comes across Dog.

00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:20.101
-Look, a doggy.
-Doggy.

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:23.187
<i>"Boss, where are you going?"</i>

00:09:23.271 --> 00:09:24.313
<i>"Dog…"</i>

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:27.149
<i>"I'm gonna spring
an all-out attack on Demon Island."</i>

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:30.820
<i>"Can you use these sweet dumplings
to recruit Monkey and Pheasant?"</i>

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:34.824
<i>He gets on a boat
with his three sworn brothers.</i>

00:09:35.575 --> 00:09:38.911
<i>"Hey, you ruthless bastards, time to pay,"</i>

00:09:38.995 --> 00:09:40.913
<i>shouted Momotaro, attacking gung ho style.</i>

00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:43.833
<i>"Who are you and what group are you from?"</i>

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:46.335
<i>"We're the Momo Group!"</i>

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:50.006
Angry roars and screams followed
in a scene straight from hell.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:53.301
In no time,
Momotaro wipes out scores of demons.

00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:56.429
<i>"Demon Boss,
you know what happens next, eh?"</i>

00:09:56.512 --> 00:09:58.889
<i>Momotaro corners the demons.</i>

00:09:58.973 --> 00:10:02.101
"Spare me, and I'll give you
all the money you want!"

00:10:02.184 --> 00:10:04.729
"Name your price. How much do you want?"

00:10:04.812 --> 00:10:06.063
"How much?"

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:06.981
CLANG

00:10:07.064 --> 00:10:08.107
<i>"Use this."</i>

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.025
<i>"What?"</i>

00:10:10.026 --> 00:10:11.861
<i>-"You know what this is, right?"
-"What…"</i>

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:12.903
RUSH

00:10:12.987 --> 00:10:14.530
-"Your finger--"
-Okay!

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:20.244
That's when the demons apologized,
and Momotaro forgave the demons.

00:10:20.328 --> 00:10:22.079
They lived happily ever after.

00:10:22.163 --> 00:10:24.206
CLAP

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:25.916
Wait a minute!

00:10:26.417 --> 00:10:29.211
We were just getting into
"the never-ending conflicts" part…

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.637
The boss, the lead henchman,
and the underlings…

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.680
Ten young lads altogether.

00:10:39.764 --> 00:10:44.018
Out of these, seven got busted.
It's a massive blow.

00:10:44.769 --> 00:10:46.604
How many are left?

00:10:46.687 --> 00:10:48.981
I got it! It's three!

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:51.317
Nicely done.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.526
Phew.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.779
So we've settled the score on Math.

00:10:55.529 --> 00:11:00.242
Who's next on your summer holiday
assignments to take down?

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:05.665
Well, Math and Japanese are done,
so now I just have Independent Research.

00:11:05.748 --> 00:11:10.378
Independent Research?
You left the baddest mother for the end.

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:14.840
You can do an experiment,
an investigation,

00:11:14.924 --> 00:11:17.343
or make something simple
like a wooden pen holder.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.763
Something out of wood… A pen holder…

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:23.516
Sorry for making you
help with this, Tatsu.

00:11:23.599 --> 00:11:25.059
This is my room!

00:11:25.142 --> 00:11:25.976
SWISH

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:29.021
First, we make a diagram.
Then we'll get the gear.

00:11:29.105 --> 00:11:30.481
SAW

00:11:30.564 --> 00:11:31.565
Pen holder…

00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:37.696
Up slightly! That's it!

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:38.697
Pen holder…

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:39.740
WHIRR

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:42.076
And we're done!

00:11:42.159 --> 00:11:43.744
Wow, it looks so stylish.

00:11:43.828 --> 00:11:48.749
Yay… But what about the pen holder?
What's with the stylish room makeover?

00:11:48.833 --> 00:11:51.669
Well, hold on.
There are several major features.

00:11:51.752 --> 00:11:54.755
I used a temp wall
so we don't harm the walls.

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:58.801
It has a walnut-like finish that matches
the colors and gives it a vintage feel.

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:01.720
It uses the space better
and provides lots of storage.

00:12:01.804 --> 00:12:05.182
The pegboard provides
both convenience and style.

00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:08.185
If you put a box here,
it can hold your pens.

00:12:08.269 --> 00:12:09.478
Wow, you're right!

00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:10.438
Okay…

00:12:11.105 --> 00:12:12.189
That's great,

00:12:12.773 --> 00:12:15.109
but this is for
an elementary school project.

00:12:15.192 --> 00:12:17.194
Maybe something smaller and less grown up?

00:12:17.278 --> 00:12:20.448
I remember that when I was at school,
I made some colorful soap.

00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:22.908
Yes, exactly, that sort of thing!

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:25.369
Colorful soap?

00:12:25.953 --> 00:12:29.331
There's this one method which is
a bit dodgy but should work.

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:31.083
Waste oil, water,

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:32.793
and caustic soda.

00:12:33.419 --> 00:12:36.755
Watch out for this one.
It's powerful stuff.

00:12:37.339 --> 00:12:40.426
First, dissolve the caustic soda
in the water.

00:12:40.509 --> 00:12:43.471
Let it cool down slowly. That's it…

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:46.474
-Then mix in the waste oil!
-That's a dirty color.

00:12:48.142 --> 00:12:49.351
Looking good.

00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:50.978
It's not colorful at all.

00:12:51.562 --> 00:12:53.856
Put the cap on firmly
and give it a good shake.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:58.068
When it turns thick and white, it's done.

00:12:58.152 --> 00:13:01.614
Now pour it into a milk carton
and wait until it sets.

00:13:01.697 --> 00:13:02.531
How long?

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:04.658
-In the summer, it takes three days.
-Okay.

00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:07.536
Once it sets, cut it out
and leave it for one month to mature.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:08.746
Right, okay.

00:13:08.829 --> 00:13:11.081
AUGUST 31

00:13:11.832 --> 00:13:13.667
<i>Today is the last day…</i>

00:13:14.418 --> 00:13:15.252
KATAGI ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

00:13:15.336 --> 00:13:17.046
<i>"So that's why I don't have
the goods to show you,</i>

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:20.758
but apparently, when this dodgy liquid
and white powder sets,

00:13:20.841 --> 00:13:23.511
you can use it on anything
and it will go white."

00:13:23.594 --> 00:13:27.348
"That's what the man said as he laughed."

00:13:33.354 --> 00:13:36.023
<i>…and then they say they don't need food
since they already ate.</i>

00:13:36.106 --> 00:13:37.274
<i>Yeah, I get that as well.</i>

00:13:37.858 --> 00:13:41.487
If you don't need dinner, tell me earlier!
I mean, I already made it.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.488
I know, right?

00:13:44.907 --> 00:13:47.409
Depending on the situation,
it can be an all-out war.

00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:50.079
Tatsu, using rough words again!

00:13:50.829 --> 00:13:52.915
But you're right, it is a war, isn't it?

00:13:52.998 --> 00:13:56.126
Oh, excuse me.
One strawberry mille crepe cake, please!

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.588
Cooking for the family everyday
is a tough job!

00:13:59.672 --> 00:14:03.217
Yeah, it was tough
when I was the resident lackey.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.301
"Lackey"?

00:14:04.969 --> 00:14:08.305
<i>One time, I had to dish up
a hundred servings of sashimi to guests.</i>

00:14:08.389 --> 00:14:09.306
<i>One hundred?</i>

00:14:09.974 --> 00:14:11.517
<i>I messed up a bit</i>

00:14:12.226 --> 00:14:14.353
<i>and almost got some "beans" blasted in me.</i>

00:14:14.853 --> 00:14:16.855
Oh, beans.

00:14:17.648 --> 00:14:18.482
Beans?

00:14:18.566 --> 00:14:20.484
-Take this, you punk!
-<i>She shot beans at you?</i>

00:14:20.568 --> 00:14:23.195
Oh, right. We've got a dog.

00:14:23.279 --> 00:14:26.240
My husband and kids looked after it
and took it on walks at first,

00:14:26.323 --> 00:14:29.076
but now I'm doing everything!

00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:30.995
Oh, yeah, I know how you feel.

00:14:31.078 --> 00:14:35.249
<i>We once had 20 dogs and I had
to walk them all at the same time.</i>

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:39.253
I love dogs, but 20 is madness!
Not to mention the costs…

00:14:39.336 --> 00:14:40.713
Twenty?

00:14:41.714 --> 00:14:42.673
<i>Wow…</i>

00:14:42.756 --> 00:14:45.759
For the husband and kids, it's easy.
They get a holiday.

00:14:45.843 --> 00:14:46.844
Exactly.

00:14:46.927 --> 00:14:49.638
We have to do the cleaning
no matter what else we've got on.

00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:52.975
<i>I had to do the cleaning
right in the middle of a full-on ambush.</i>

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:53.893
<i>Ambush?</i>

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.603
-You asshole!
-<i>What on earth?</i>

00:14:55.686 --> 00:14:58.355
<i>Things got hot
and the dining table got flipped over.</i>

00:14:58.439 --> 00:15:02.610
<i>I was told to bring the lotus roots
but then got smacked for it.</i>

00:15:03.235 --> 00:15:05.112
<i>-Is that what Miku is like?
-Is that what Miku is like?</i>

00:15:05.195 --> 00:15:07.031
A bit different to how she looks…

00:15:07.114 --> 00:15:07.990
Right?

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:10.034
Sorry, my wife is calling.

00:15:10.117 --> 00:15:12.953
Hey, Tacchan. Are you busy?

00:15:13.037 --> 00:15:14.914
I got off work and I'm going home now.

00:15:14.997 --> 00:15:16.749
Yes, ma'am. You must have had a long day.

00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:17.666
GULP

00:15:18.292 --> 00:15:21.670
I was just thinking, I feel like having
some homemade udon tonight.

00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.297
Have you made dinner already?

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.799
This evening…
Yeah, I can cut 'em up for you.

00:15:26.926 --> 00:15:28.010
"Cut 'em up"?

00:15:28.594 --> 00:15:34.433
It's no biggie. Just need to prepare
some of that white powder.

00:15:34.516 --> 00:15:35.392
<i>-Here we go.
-Here we go.</i>

00:15:35.476 --> 00:15:38.729
Some tempura
and summer veggies would be good too.

00:15:38.812 --> 00:15:39.980
Maybe some green peppers?

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:43.192
Oh, that would mean burning them up.

00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:44.401
<i>-There it is.
-There it is.</i>

00:15:44.985 --> 00:15:50.366
Well, boiling 'em or burning 'em is fine.
Yes… Got it.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.868
Well, you get the goods in then.

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:56.538
<i>-What's going on with this couple?
-What's going on with this couple?</i>

00:15:58.916 --> 00:16:01.585
<i>Tea time was fun, ladies.</i>

00:16:01.669 --> 00:16:03.337
Sorry about the phone call.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.839
What? Oh, that's totally fine.

00:16:06.423 --> 00:16:10.511
It sounded a bit complicated…
Everything all right?

00:16:10.594 --> 00:16:14.056
Oh, Miku's asking me
to help pound something.

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:15.808
I need to go and sort that out.

00:16:15.891 --> 00:16:20.187
Tatsu, if you have any trouble,
you can always come to us.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.355
Take these sweets.

00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:24.400
<i>-The Way of the Househusband.
-The Way of the Househusband.</i>

00:16:26.443 --> 00:16:29.363
And before he could react,
I smacked him one.

00:16:29.947 --> 00:16:32.491
The frog started blubbering like a baby.

00:16:32.574 --> 00:16:34.576
Wow, you're so tough!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.996
I've never once lost a fight.

00:16:37.579 --> 00:16:40.958
If a punch comes here, do this.
If a punch comes there, do that. See?

00:16:41.041 --> 00:16:42.042
Okay, so…

00:16:42.126 --> 00:16:44.044
SMACK, BAM

00:16:44.128 --> 00:16:45.295
That hurts!

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:46.505
Stop that!

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:49.341
Surprise attacks are not allowed. Stop.

00:16:49.925 --> 00:16:52.886
A fight is a fair contest of strength,
done by the book.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:53.929
I see!

00:16:54.013 --> 00:16:54.888
CROUCH

00:16:55.514 --> 00:16:56.348
C'mon then.

00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:58.809
What? Afterimages?

00:16:59.393 --> 00:17:00.310
Where are you going?

00:17:00.394 --> 00:17:01.228
RUSTLE

00:17:01.311 --> 00:17:02.187
Huh?

00:17:02.271 --> 00:17:03.105
CHOMP

00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:04.064
Ouch!

00:17:04.148 --> 00:17:06.108
Idiot! Not from behind!

00:17:06.692 --> 00:17:08.861
Jeez, so many requests.
